    {
      "index": 2,
      "id": "problem",
      "heading": "Problem",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c1_imitation_learning_self_driving_cars",
          "text": "\"Imitation learning for self-driving cars is usually done through behavioral cloning, where the network is trained to reproduce an expert's next action.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "imitation",
            "learning",
            "self-driving",
            "cars",
            "usually",
            "done",
            "through",
            "behavioral",
            "cloning",
            "where"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_catch_done_open_loop_never_sees",
          "text": "The catch is that this is done open-loop: the model never sees the consequences of its own actions. But when the policy actually drives, every action changes the future state it will see.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "catch",
            "done",
            "open-loop",
            "never",
            "sees",
            "consequences",
            "its",
            "own",
            "actions",
            "but"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_small_prediction_errors_accumulate_p",
          "text": "Small prediction errors accumulate, pushing the car into out-of-distribution situations the model was never trained on.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "small",
            "prediction",
            "errors",
            "accumulate",
            "pushing",
            "car",
            "out-of-distribution",
            "situations",
            "never",
            "trained"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c4_metrics_truly_matter_like_collisions",
          "text": "And the metrics that truly matter, like collisions, are non-differentiable, so they are effectively invisible to the standard training loss. The result is a policy that looks great open-loop but drives poorly in closed-loop evaluation.\"",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "metrics",
            "truly",
            "matter",
            "like",
            "collisions",
            "non-differentiable",
            "they",
            "effectively",
            "invisible",
