          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s08_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s08_c2_combining_front_side_distance_to_ref",
          "text": "Combining front, side, and distance-to-reference works nicely, but adding rear collisions causes a clear regression. The authors trace this to false positives in the rear-collision metric, caused by log-replayed agents that do not react in the simulator. Two hyperparameters also matter.",
